     3	**P1 — [.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:9184](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:9184), [.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:9191](<WT>/.claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:9191)** — the context-pressure GC deletes adopter-owned dotfiles. It strips one leading `.` before its broad prefix check, so an old regular file such as `.claude/state/.context-pressure-last-bucket.adopter-notes` is treated as a framework crash-temporary and unlinked. In an unmodified eight-shard cycle, the reproduction deleted it after five sweeps. The repository still satisfied condition 28’s real-directory/type checks, while its reserved-name list omits this leading-dot namespace at [CONDITIONS-rc1.md:567](<WT>/.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1/CONDITIONS-rc1.md:567). Minimal fix: stop stripping the dot and leave crash temporaries unswept for rc.1, or add the dot-prefixed namespace to a newly signed condition and repeat the re-pass.
