.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:7:   **Concrete failure scenario:** the diff claims the hot path performs three `getenv` calls, but lines 186–189 unconditionally perform four. More importantly, the reviewer contract requires rejection of added throughput/speed claims. Condition 38 acknowledges the false statement but defers it, which cannot waive that rule.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:17:   **Minimal fix:** qualify both comments as excluding only the slug and salt-path payload values, matching the corrected SPEC and dispatch comment; alternatively, remove the false “CURADO” assertion from condition 23.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:31:   **Concrete failure scenario:** both comments say the event determines whether “THIS session” modified memory. The directory is project-shared: a concurrent session’s write inside the observation window can make this session emit `written`. This can produce false forensic attribution. Condition 20 describes the behavior correctly but condition 38 omits these two stale sites.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:33:   **Minimal fix:** say “activity occurred in the shared project memory directory during this session’s window; no session authorship is proven,” and add the sites to condition 38 until corrected.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:41:   **Minimal fix:** make the top-level text conditional on enforcement and name `ledger_entry_rejected` as the durable action. Add this to condition 24; the module remains dormant outside tests in this rc.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r12/verdict-rc1-6.txt:47:VERDICT: NO-GO — Remove the prohibited performance claim and correct condition 23’s incomplete cure assertion before rc.1, then carry findings 3–5 as explicit P2 residuals in the signed envelope.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:5:   **Concrete failure scenario:** condition 27 recommends copying the entire shared v1.3 `state/` directory, but that directory contains audit crash-recovery files as well as plan SQLite stores. If repository B previously crashed leaving `audit-spool.<dead-pid>.jsonl`, copying the directory for repository A imports that spool into A’s new per-project state. The candidate drainer accepts it without project binding, removes its prior HMAC fields, re-chains it with A’s key, and appends it to A’s log. This recreates cross-project audit contamination inside the supposedly isolated chain; some affected actions are not even attributable by their event fields. It also conflicts with condition 68’s requirement that the new `state` name be absent before first use.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:6:   **Minimal fix:** remove the whole-directory-copy route from condition 27 and the upgrade guide. For rc.1, require `CEO_PROJECT_NAME=ceo-orchestration` until the active plan closes. Any migration must selectively copy the named plan’s SQLite data and must first drain or quarantine all legacy `audit-spool*` and `audit-pending*` files using the v1.3 chain.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:10:   **Concrete failure scenario:** condition 28 guards only the `.claude/state` directory, not the new leaves. A normal, single-linked adopter file `.claude/state/.gc-shard-cursor` passes every stated preflight, then the first armed pressure transition replaces it unconditionally with `os.replace`. PostCompact similarly unlinks any homonymous context marker without proving the framework created it, while GC deletes any aged file matching the prefix. A FIFO at the fixed cursor or marker path blocks in `read_text()` instead of failing open.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:11:   **Minimal fix:** add a hard rc.1 condition requiring `.gc-shard-cursor`, `context-pressure-last-bucket`, and `context-pressure-last-bucket.*` to contain no adopter-owned objects before hooks run. The code fix is a dedicated, provenance-established framework directory plus `lstat`/directory-descriptor operations that preserve unproved leaves.
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:20:   **Concrete failure scenario:** the new docstring claims the hot path performs three `getenv` calls, but the implementation unconditionally performs four. This is both unreproducible and prohibited by the repository’s no-speed-claim reviewer contract.  
.claude/plans/PLAN-169/repass-rc1-20260908-NOGO/r11/verdict-rc1-6.txt:25:VERDICT: NO-GO — Conditions 27 and 28 permit cross-project audit contamination and destructive takeover of adopter-authored state leaves, so the proposed signed envelope is not sufficient for rc.1.
