   416	def write_last_hmac(digest: bytes) -> None:
   417	    """Persist the last HMAC to the sidecar (best-effort, no fsync).
   418	
   419	    Performance-engineer review §10 red flag #1: a second fsync under
   420	    the lock doubles variance. The sidecar is reconstructible from
   421	    log tail so skipping fsync is the right trade-off. If the sidecar
   422	    is corrupt or absent after a crash, :func:`read_prev_hmac` returns
   423	    genesis and the chain reseals on next write (operator sees a
   424	    one-line break in verify-chain, distinguishable from tamper via
   425	    monotonic ``ts``).
