8) — EDGE-TRIGGERED context-pressure breadcrumb: the session crossed INTO a new context-usage percent rung. A TRANSITION, never a per-turn sample — the hysteresis gate is `audit_emit.should_emit_context_pressure(used_bucket, state_dir)`, which persists the last rung in the marker `context-pressure-last-bucket` under the gitignored `.claude/state/` and FAILS OPEN (any state I/O error means “emit”: a bookkeeping file may never block or crash a user session, and fail-CLOSED here would silently lose the very signal PLAN-179 exists to measure). Without that gate the rail would append one row per prompt while the session sits in a single rung. Off-enum input never re-arms the marker — a bogus value must not be able to suppress the NEXT real transition. Emitted via `emit_generic` (no public typed wrapper — the `settings_tamper_detected` / compaction-pair precedent). Routes through the dedicated `_scrub_*` branch + `_CONTEXT_PRESSURE_OBSERVED_ALLOWLIST`, NEVER `_EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH`. DENIED on the wire: the raw token/byte counts, the exact percentage (a precise figure is a side channel on session size — the rung is the governance signal), the transcript text, the plan PATH text, the prompt body. NO ATLAS technique (governance/observability breadcrumb, not a detection signal). |
