  9059	    numbers hash alike), so a plain membership test would wave a FLOAT onto
  9060	    the wire — and a float under the HMAC chain DISCARDS THE WHOLE EVENT
  9061	    (S181 / ADR-055-AMEND-2), not just the offending field. ``bool`` is
  9062	    rejected explicitly because it is an ``int`` subclass and ``True`` would
  9063	    otherwise sail through any numeric check.
  9064	    """
  9065	    if isinstance(value, bool) or not isinstance(value, int):
  9066	        return False
