   630	
   631	### Rollback B — git revert + re-install
   632	
   633	If you committed any framework files (e.g. a settings.json change),
   634	revert the commit and re-install:
   635	
   636	```bash
   637	git log --oneline -- .claude/ | head -5
   638	git revert <upgrade-commit-sha>
   639	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin <previous-version>
   640	```
   641	
   642	### After rollback
   643	
   644	Run validate-governance + ceo-health to confirm:
   645	
   646	```bash
   647	bash .claude/scripts/validate-governance.sh
   648	python3 .claude/scripts/ceo-health.py
   649	```
   650	
   651	Then file an issue against the framework with the failure mode
   652	that forced the rollback.
   653	
   654	## Adopter override preservation
   655	
   656	Per ADR-052 §Adopter override, `upgrade.sh` preserves your
   657	customizations to:
   658	
   659	- `.claude/agents/<canonical-5>.md` — `model:` field, additional
   660	  `tools:` entries, prompt body customizations
   661	- `.claude/team.md`, `.claude/frontend-team.md` — your concrete
   662	  personas, project-specific routing, custom approvers
   663	- `.claude/skills/domains/<your-domain>/` — your domain content
   664	- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` — your project context
   665	- `.claude/settings.json` — only the parts you've customized; new
   666	  base hooks added during upgrade
   667	
   668	What `upgrade.sh` will overwrite:
   669	
   670	- `.claude/skills/core/` — universal skills shipped by framework
   671	- `.claude/skills/frontend/` — universal frontend skills
   672	- `.claude/hooks/` — all hooks
   673	- `.claude/scripts/` — framework-shipped scripts
   674	- `.claude/commands/` — universal slash commands
   675	
   676	If you have customized anything in the "will overwrite" list,
   677	either:
   678	
   679	1. Move your customization to `domains/<your-domain>/` (preserved)
   680	2. Maintain a fork of the framework
   681	3. Submit your customization upstream as a PR
   682	
   683	## Schema migrations (audit log etc.)
   684	
   685	The audit log is **additive within v1** — new versions add fields
   686	but never remove or rename. Your existing audit-log.jsonl reads
   687	fine after an upgrade. Specifically:
   688	
   689	| Audit-log SPEC version | Added in framework version | What's new |
   690	|-------------------------|------------------------------|------------|
   691	| v2.0 | `v1.0.0-rc.1` | Five typed events: agent_spawn, debate_event, plan_transition, veto_triggered, benchmark_run |
   692	| v2.1 | Sprint 5 | injection_flag |
   693	| v2.2 | Sprint 8 | confidence_gate, lesson_read/archived/restored, lesson_outcome |
   694	| v2.3 | Sprint 9 | lesson_outcome_undone |
   695	| v2.4 | Sprint 11 | state_store_*, budget_*, otel_export_dropped, output_safety_flag, skill_patch_applied, squad_imported |
   696	| v2.5 | Sprint 13 | live_adapter_*, breaker_*, credential_rotation_due, mcp_handler_* |
   697	| v2.6 | Sprint 14 | policy_*, replay_*, prediction_queried, pattern_*, threat_model_* |
   698	| v2.7 | Sprint 32 (PLAN-020) | usage_metadata, cache_coverage, rail (additive on agent_spawn) |
   699	| v2.8 | Sprint 32 (PLAN-021) | model (additive on agent_spawn) |
   700	
   701	Per `SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md` §Consumer contract, consumers
   702	tolerate unknown fields. Your `audit-query.py` from a newer install
   703	reads logs from older installs without issue. The reverse may
   704	ignore fields silently.
   705	
   706	## Upgrade examples (real)
   707	
   708	### `v1.10.0` → `v1.11.x` (Claude-only refocus, audit-v2 readiness ladder)
   709	
   710	The v1.10.0 → v1.11.x line is **mid-pivot** (audit-v2 verdict
   711	`TRIAL-PENDING-SOAK`). v1.11.0 reframed the framework from
   712	multi-adapter (Gemini + OpenAI + local) to **Claude-only** (ADR-084
   713	+ ADR-085). Adopters who installed against `v1.10.0` should expect:
   714	
   715	- Adapter stubs deleted (`gemini.py`, `openai.py`, `local.py`)
   716	- `validate.yml::adapter-matrix` job removed
   717	- 5 plans re-opened `done → executing` per ADR-092 honest-deferral
   718	- New ADRs (092 honest-deferral, 093 60-day refused-ADR moratorium)
   719	- Calendar-soak gates active — 14-day CI green + 30-day no-retag
   720	  + 60-day refused-ADR moratorium (gates earliest TRIAL 2026-06-26)
   721	
   722	```bash
   723	cd /path/to/adopter-project
   724	
   725	# Pre
   726	bash .claude/scripts/ceo-backup.sh
   727	git status   # clean
   728	
   729	# Verify framework's own CI is green at the target tag
   730	gh run list --repo Canhada-Labs/ceo-orchestration \
   731	  --workflow validate.yml --branch main --limit 3
   732	# All three should be green. v1.11.1 had a known release.yml red
   733	# (VERSION/tag mismatch); v1.11.2 is the first clean tag in the
   734	# v1.11 line.
   735	
   736	# Upgrade
   737	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.11.2
   738	
   739	# Post
   740	bash .claude/scripts/validate-governance.sh   # PASS
   741	ls .claude/hooks/_lib/adapters/
   742	# expect ONLY: __init__.py, claude.py
   743	# (gemini.py, openai.py, local.py DELETED per ADR-084)
   744	
   745	python3 .claude/scripts/audit-query.py recent --limit 1
   746	# expect 'model' + 'rail' + 'usage_metadata' fields
   747	
   748	python3 .claude/scripts/ceo-health.py   # exit 0
   749	```
   750	
   751	If your project had any references to the deleted adapter stubs
   752	(unlikely — they were stubs for parity tests, not user-facing),
   753	remove them. Otherwise the upgrade is non-breaking.
   754	
   755	### `v1.5.0-rc.1` → `v1.6.0-rc.1` (legacy reference)
   756	
   757	```bash
   758	cd /path/to/adopter-project
   759	
   760	# Pre
   761	bash .claude/scripts/ceo-backup.sh
   762	git status   # clean
   763	
   764	# Upgrade
   765	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.6.0-rc.1
   766	
   767	# Post
   768	bash .claude/scripts/validate-governance.sh   # PASS
   769	ls .claude/agents/   # 5 canonical-5 + _dispatch.md (NEW from PLAN-020)
   770	python3 .claude/scripts/audit-query.py recent --limit 1
   771	# expect 'model' + 'rail' + 'usage_metadata' fields
   772	python3 .claude/scripts/ceo-health.py   # exit 0
   773	```
   774	
   775	If your project hadn't installed the canonical-5 native agents
   776	before (because your existing install predates `v1.6.0-rc.1`),
   777	the upgrade adds them. Customize via the `.claude/agents/<slug>.md`
   778	frontmatter as needed.
   779	
   780	### Custom: pin to a specific RC during evaluation
   781	
   782	```bash
   783	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.11.2
   784	
   785	# Run for a week against your real workload
   786	# If happy and 14-day CI green streak holds:
   787	bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.11.x    # promote to GA when audit-v3 + soak windows clear
   788	```
   789	
   790	The `--pin` flag is **one-shot**: a subsequent `bash scripts/upgrade.sh`
   791	without `--pin` follows the source checkout's current default branch, not
   792	the version you pinned. Pass `--pin` on every upgrade to hold a version
   793	(see `VERSIONING.md` §Adopter pinning).
   794	
   795	## Coordinating an upgrade across a team
   796	
   797	If multiple engineers share the framework install:
   798	
   799	1. **Notify the team** before upgrading: "I'm bumping framework
   800	   from `v1.10.0` to `v1.11.2` on Tuesday."
   801	2. **Upgrade in a feature branch**:
   802	   ```bash
   803	   git checkout -b chore/framework-v1.11.2
   804	   bash scripts/upgrade.sh --pin v1.11.2
   805	   git add .claude/
   806	   git commit -m "chore: upgrade framework to v1.11.2"
   807	   git push origin chore/framework-v1.11.2
   808	   ```
   809	3. **Merge with full CI green** — the framework upgrade may
   810	   surface previously-quiet test issues.
   811	4. **Communicate the merge**: "Framework upgraded; rebase your
   812	   feature branches; new env vars in `docs/CHEAT-SHEET.md`."
   813	
   814	## When NOT to upgrade
   815	
   816	- During an active sprint deadline (delay until post-ship)
   817	- When you have an open SEV-2+ incident (upgrade adds variables)
   818	- During a freeze period your team has agreed on
   819	- When the target is a GA tag cut < 24h after its RC (the ADR-103
   820	  Codex re-pass window isn't done)
   821	- When the framework's own CI is currently red on the target tag
   822	  (wait for the fix-up RC)
   823	
